  data: {
    LLM: 'Each player receives 4 tiles and must split them into a High Hand (2 tiles) and a Low Hand (2 tiles). The High Hand must rank at least equal to the Low Hand according to standard Pai Gow tile rankings. After all players have set their hands, the Banker reveals their 4 tiles and forms their high and low hands.',
    Player: 'Each player receives 4 tiles and must split them into a High Hand (2 tiles) and a Low Hand (2 tiles). The High Hand must rank at least equal to the Low Hand according to standard Pai Gow tile rankings. After all players have set their hands, the Banker reveals their 4 tiles and forms their high and low hands.',
    objective: "Form two hands (high hand and low hand) from your 4 tiles that both beat the Banker's corresponding hands.",
    gameplay: 'Each player receives 4 tiles and must split them into a High Hand (2 tiles) and a Low Hand (2 tiles). The High Hand must rank at least equal to the Low Hand according to standard Pai Gow tile rankings. After all players have set their hands, the Banker reveals their 4 tiles and forms their high and low hands.',
    keyRules: [
